ansible 


ansible lab
take two instance ec2
allow http traffic in both
deb1
sudo apt update
sudo apt install ansible -y
ansible --version
ssh -V ->if not present then-apt install openssh-client -y

create ssh-keygen
copy public key from deb1 and paste it in deb2 in .ssh->nano authorized_keys paste here deb1 pub key
then set permission of .ssh to 700 like this ->sudo chmod 700 .ssh

IN deb2 
sudo apt update
sudo apt install openssh-server python3 -y
sudo systemctl enable --now ssh
sudo systemctl status ssh

test deb2user@deb2id
it should access without asking password,passwordless

create anventory on debian1

mkdir -p ansible-lab
cd ansible-lab
nano inventory.ini
   |
[debian_servers]
Deb2ip ansible_user=deb2name

save it
expected ping pong

nano setup_apache.yml
        |
---
- name: Update deb2 and install apache2
  hosts: debian_servers
  become: true
  tasks:
   - name: refresh apt
     ansible.builtin.apt:
        update_cache: true
   - name: upgrade install
     ansible.builtin.apt:
        upgrade: yes
   - name: create user
     ansible.builtin.user:
        name: tinku
        group: admin
   - name: install
     ansible.builtin.apt:
        name: tree
        state: present
   - name: install apache2
     ansible.builtin.apt:
        name: apache2
        state: present
 
 save it
 

run in deb1

->ansible-playbook -i inventory.ini setup_apache2.yml 

from this big process starts

to check apache2
ansible -i inventory.ini debian_servers -b -m command -a "apache2 -v"

